==Battleground==
*1 [[Spacefish Jones]] spawns as the boss after 1.67 seconds<sup>50f</sup>.
*1 [[Star Peng]] spawns after 1.67 seconds<sup>50f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage's difficulty drops dramatically with more than one chapter's worth of [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]], so, if you struggle or don't want want to risk wasting [[Cat Energy|energy]], get some/more of them before attempting this stage. Just wait for the Star Peng to get near your base and start spamming meatshields and some attackers. After Spacefish Jones dies, spawn [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to destroy the enemy base before the Li'l Bun Buns appear.

If you only have the Anti-Starred Alien Treasures from [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 1, it will be useful to bring [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or other [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Anti-Floating]]/high DPS units, as odds are you won't be able to clear the stage before the Li'l Bun Buns start appearing.

A second strategy could be to stall the stage out using 3 meatshields, Can Can Cat to kill the Star Pengs and Fishman Cat to kill the Li'l Bun Buns while stacking [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyperpunk Cats]] and other cats with over 840 range to kill Spacefish Jones. Once Spacefish Jones is dead, the stage is practically over and it's just a matter of getting to the base. This strategy become dramatically easier with >500% Anti-Starred Alien Treasures but can be done with minimal Treasures if your cats have high enough levels (most cats around level 40).

==Trivia==
*In real life, the [[wikipedia:Tunguska event|Tunguska event]] was an enormous explosion that occurred near the Stony Tunguska River in Yeniseysk Governorate, Russia, on the morning of 30 June 1908. Though believed to have been caused by the airburst of a small comet or meteorite, science fiction often attributes the event to [[:Category:Alien Enemies|aliens]], such as in the short story "[[wikipedia:The Second Missile|The Second Missile]]".

